      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It is completely understandable that the idea of \"strategies\" feels pointless when your core sense of reality is shaky. The emptiness you describe is the raw feeling of disconnection, and it's a heavy burden to carry. Instead of trying to force yourself to feel something, perhaps focus on the simple, undeniable physical acts—the weight of your chair, the temperature of the air—as small anchors in the noise. Even tiny moments of tangible sensation can be a quiet way to remind yourself that *something* is present.",
      "source": "target",
